// Native canonical-IPA data manifest for Tashelhit / Shilha (shi) — Taclḥit, a Berber (Amazigh) language of
// SW Morocco (Souss), ~7–9M. Consumed by tashelhit.ts. Input = the Berber Latin alphabet (the academic/community
// Latin orthography; Tifinagh + Arabic are the other scripts). The orthography is near-1:1 PHONEMIC: a greedy
// grapheme scan + two rules — LABIALISATION (a consonant + ⟨ʷ⟩ → Cʷ) and GEMINATION (a doubled letter → a long
// consonant Cː, phonemic in Berber). Emphatics = pharyngealised (dot-below): ḍ→dˤ ṭ→tˤ ṣ→sˤ ẓ→zˤ ṛ→rˤ; pharyngeals
// ḥ→ħ ɛ→ʕ; uvulars ɣ→ʁ~ɣ, x→χ, q; ⟨c⟩→ʃ, ⟨j⟩→ʒ, ⟨y⟩→j, ⟨e⟩→ə. Maps derived from wikipron shi_latn + kaikki
// Tashelhit (both Wiktionary → correlated single-source-family). See docs/investigations/shi_native_bringup_investigation.md.
